{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,120p' collab/findings.md; sed -n '1,120p' collab/brief.md; rg -n 'qualified-keyword\\\\?|keyword\\\\?' src/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc; rg -n 'run-compile-output|compile-command-ast' test/yin/repl*; rg -n 'a toy frontend|frontend-catalog-test' deps.edn shadow-cljs.edn project.clj package.json\"","aggregated_output":"# Findings: yang.python Phase C4 Slice F2 (REPL catalog selection)\n\nEngineer: claude-sonnet-5-5. Not committed (collab/ is never staged).\n\n## Implemented\n- `src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc` (new): `standard` builds the default\n  `yang.frontend` catalog (`:yang.clojure/legacy`, `:yang.python/legacy`,\n  `:yang.php/legacy`, languages `:clojure :python :php`). It is the only\n  place the REPL composition requires `yang.clojure/python/php`.\n  Binding shape: `{:parse f :lower f}` plus `:input :forms` for Clojure,\n  whose reader stays the shell's own.\n- `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc`:\n  - Dropped the static `yang.clojure/php/python` requires; requires\n    `yang.frontend` and `yin.repl.frontends`.\n  - `create-state` takes `:frontends` (default `(repl.frontends/standard)`),\n    stored as `:frontends`, an immutable snapshot pinned by the session.\n  - The closed `case` in `compile-source` / `compile-command-ast` /\n    `eval-parsed*` is replaced by catalog dispatch (`select-frontend`,\n    `frontend-binding`, `compile-input`).\n  - `:lang` is a qualified id (`:yang.python/legacy`) or a language keyword\n    (`:python`, which must name exactly one installed id).\n  - An id or language not in the catalog, or a binding without parse and\n    lower, throws an `unavailable-parser` diagnostic. There is no fallback.\n    `(lang :yang.python/antlr)` answers `Error: unavailable-parser: ...`\n    and leaves `:lang` unchanged.\n- `test/yin/repl/frontend_catalog_test.cljc`: 4 tests. A toy frontend is\n  selected by language and by id and evaluates on all four VMs. The\n  standard languages still work. A newer revision leaves a live session\n  unchanged. An unavailable id answers unavailable-parser with no legacy\n  result.\n\n## Verification\n- JVM: `clojure -M:test -n yin.repl.frontend-catalog-test`: 4 tests, 26\n  assertions, 0 failures. `yin.repl-test`, `main-test` and `adapter-test`:\n  98 tests, 634 assertions, 0 failures.\n- Node: `bb test:cljs`: 3811 tests, 108192 assertions, 0 failures. The\n  frontend-catalog namespace ran.\n- Dart: `bb test:cljd`: \"All tests passed!\". The namespace is in the\n  aggregated shard list, but the compact reporter printed no per-test lines\n  for it, so I could not confirm its tests individually.\n- `clj -M:kondo` on the three touched files: 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n\n## Notes and deviations\n- `bb test:clj -n <ns>` does not forward `-n`: the task ignores arguments\n  and runs the whole suite plus builds. I stopped it and used\n  `clojure -M:test -n <ns>` for the targeted JVM run.\n- Behaviour change: `(lang :bogus)` now answers\n  `Error: unavailable-parser: ...` instead of `Unknown Yin REPL language ...`.\n  No tests or docs referenced the old text.\n- The brief's Node/Dart item \"ANTLR id unavailable with no parser\" is\n  covered by the default catalog holding no `:yang.python/antlr`, so the\n  same assertion runs on every host. Installing a real ANTLR binding into\n  a composition is later work (F3/P-slices).\n- Not done: no revision-pinned `:lang` form (selection without a revision\n  is ambiguous if several revisions of one id are installed, and surfaces\n  as unavailable-parser). The completeness probe from the spec is not wired.\n- `collab/brief.md` is untracked and was left in place.\nCreated-GMT: 2026-10-09 10:50:46 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-09 17:50:46 ICT\nCoding-Agent: claude\nSession-ID: d30e62c3-3a3d-4f32-aceb-5e1e7fbba847\n\n# Task: yang.python Phase C4 Slice F2 (REPL dynamic frontend catalog selection)\nRole: Compiler Engineer / VM Engineer\nImplementers:\n- Model: claude-sonnet-5-5 | Assigned: 2026-10-09 17:50:46 ICT | Status: active | Rationale: Lead Engineer for Track 2 (Slice F2 REPL Catalog Decoupling)\n\nYou are the Engineer implementing Track 2 (Phase C4 Slice F2) in the dedicated worktree:\n`/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/yang-python-c4-f2`\n\n## Governing Architecture & Rules\n- Governing Specification: `docs/design/yang.antlr.md` (§8.5.6 Imports, the linked prelude, and the frontend catalog; Ruling 16).\n- Catalog Foundation: `src/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc` (Landed in Slice F1).\n- REPL Implementation: `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc`.\n\n## Scope of Slice F2 (Section 8.5.6)\n1. **Decouple `yin.repl` from hardcoded frontends**:\n   - `yin.repl` today has a closed `case` over three languages (`:clojure`, `:python`, `:php`) with static namespace requires.\n   - Per Ruling 16:\n     - The REPL takes the frontend catalog from its composition as a `create-state` option (defaulting to the standard catalog).\n     - A session pins an immutable catalog snapshot.\n     - `compile-source` / `compile-command-ast` dispatches through the catalog's installed binding for the selected `[id revision]`, calling parse and lower stages.\n     - Language-specific parsing and completeness logic stay out of REPL core.\n     - Drop static requires of `yang.python`, `yang.php`, etc., from `yin.repl.cljc` where they are replaced by catalog bindings.\n2. **Catalog Selection Semantics**:\n   - Support selecting frontends by keyword/id (e.g. `:clojure`, `:yang.python/legacy`, `:yang.python/antlr`).\n   - If an unconfigured or unavailable frontend is selected, answer with `unavailable-parser` diagnostic without legacy fallback.\n3. **Tests (`test/yin/repl/frontend_catalog_test.cljc`)**:\n   - A toy frontend defined in a test namespace installs, is selected, and evaluates on every VM with no `src` edit.\n   - A newer revision installed under a live session leaves it unchanged (session immutability).\n   - On Node and Dart with no parser or configured service, an unavailable parser answers with diagnostic and no fallback.\n   - Run tests across JVM (`bb test:clj -n yin.repl.frontend-catalog-test`), Node (`bb test:cljs`), and Dart (`bb test:cljd`).\n   - Clean linter (`clj -M:kondo`).\n\n## Reporting\nDeliver the complete implementation, verify across all three hosts, and record your findings in:\n`collab/1791543046262-compiler-engineer-c4-f2.claude-sonnet-5-5.findings.md`\n66:  (cond (or (nil? x) (boolean? x) (string? x) (keyword? x) (symbol? x)\n84:  (or (keyword? x) (and (string? x) (seq x))))\n90:  [[:yang.frontend/id qualified-keyword?]\n93:   [:yang.frontend/language keyword?]\n107:   [:yang.grammar/export-profile keyword?]])\nrg: project.clj: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
